A||||9||baptistheart||84 decklid||||5||
Z||000000||baptistheart||05-31-2001||12:25 AM||||I'm thinking of puting an 84 decklid on my 85 coupe. Thinking that it might help cool the engine compartment is their any reason that g.m. went from center to sides on the vents? was it a design flaw on the 84? will i adversly affect the air flow of the compartment? i figured it was designed this way for a reason but thought it might be better with more vents.<P>------------------<BR>Joe||||reg||5
Z||000001||sqoach||05-31-2001||12:30 AM||||I have an 84 decklid. Shipping would be pretty expensive though.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||05-31-2001||12:43 AM||||Well, the official reason for the redesign is to have clearance for the V6 in later years.  The expense of the Magnesium alloy vent on the 84 may have been another reason.||||reg||1
Z||000003||baptistheart||05-31-2001||12:49 AM||||Thanks. and sorry but i have my own little 84 parts car to bad have an 85 driver.<P>------------------<BR>Joe||||reg||6
Z||000004||cadaver||05-31-2001||03:55 AM||||If the 85 is a four cylinder it will work. Not if its a 6||||reg||1
Z||000005||LZeitgeist||05-31-2001||07:21 AM||||If you use the '84 decklid and the '85 side vents, it may look strange because the 'slats' in the vents go front-to-back in the decklid, and side-to-side on the side vents... if you're O.K. with that, cool, but I thought I'd point that out before you went to all the trouble of swapping decklids...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||SteveJ||05-31-2001||09:58 AM||||Its gunna rain on your engine. One of my pet peeves about the 84. Water runs down the firewall side all over the starter, sometimes fills the sparkplug holes.||||reg||1
Z||000007||DecadenceR||05-31-2001||10:29 AM||||I have an 84 with the vents in the decklid, and i want to update to the newer one. Every time it rains and I'm driving, my rear windshield fogs up like crazy, and I have no defrosters.<BR>I used to have an 87 4-cyl and I never had that problem.||||reg||1
Z||000008||beachbomb||05-31-2001||03:55 PM||||I heard the reason they changed deck lids from 84 to 85 was because in '84 the slots in the deck-lid let leaves, and other things get down into the exhaust/cat converter, and lets water in on the engine, kinda makes sense...hope it helps..jim(2 '84 Indys)||||reg||4
Z||000009||Songman||06-01-2001||09:56 PM||||I hate raising the lid on my Indy! Pours water all over everything!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 06-01-2001).]||||reg||1
